{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/140172-changeling-the-dreaming-alternate-dates-and-or-trigger-points-for-the-resurgence","id":140172,"title":"[Changeling: the Dreaming] Alternate dates and/or trigger points for the Resurgence?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-16T20:06:31-07:00","id":140172,"title":"[Changeling: the Dreaming] Alternate dates and/or trigger points for the Resurgence?","content":"So... I'm working on a Changeling chronicle, and I'm planning on using modern Orlando, FL, as my setting, but I'm thinking I'd like to run an alternate Resurgence and Accordance War chronicle. Any suggestions for what might have touched off the Resurgence instead of the 1969 moon landing? The first thing that comes to mind is either the release of <i>Harry Potter and the Philosopher's (Sorcerer's) Stone</i> or the date that said book hit the NYT Best Seller's List...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2980,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2980-steampunkadventurer","user":"SteampunkAdventurer","date":". 05-16-2014, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2980-steampunkadventurer","name":"SteampunkAdventurer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T20:20:24-07:00","id":140181,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Maybe the Mars landing of the Curiosity rover? Or you could stretch your world's reality and say that we just did our first manned mission to Mars. Or make up something else entirely. If you're looking to have the Accordance War take place in the modern era, you could just say, &quot;Poof! The gates of Arcadia opened!&quot; and call it good. <br /> <br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T07:45:48-07:00","id":140491,"title":"","content":"9-11 might be a good date. Granted, it's not the same type of &quot;dream&quot; that those other dates suggest, but it's still resonating down through the years. Imagine the weird Nightmares that were given birth <i>that</i> day.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the Mars landings are a good time, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T19:21:53-07:00","id":145140,"title":"","content":"Could also tie it into the week of nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T21:16:10-07:00","id":145264,"title":"","content":"Any seemingly impossible event that caused enough people to reawaken their belief in wonder, and/or requestion what IS possible. The fall of the Berlin Wall, for example. Or the Backstreet Boys reunion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T04:06:50-07:00","id":146569,"title":"","content":"My Nocker insists that it was <i>not</i> the Moon Landing that triggered the resurgence.<br /> <br /> Oh no, that's just what the sidhe want you to believe, that htey are a returning kith, summoned back by hte higher aspirations of mankind. but it's a sham! A phony!<br /> <br /> No, the Sidhe are a new kith, born of the dreams of <b>DISCO</b>. The big shoulders, the hair, the overbearing nature, the lack of substance, the fact that htey fare poorly in the modern world? They're all about disco.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:38:10-07:00","id":154460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Big Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/140172-changeling-the-dreaming-alternate-dates-and-or-trigger-points-for-the-resurgence?p=140491#post140491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9-11 might be a good date. Granted, it's not the same type of &quot;dream&quot; that those other dates suggest, but it's still resonating down through the years. Imagine the weird Nightmares that were given birth <i>that</i> day.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the Mars landings are a good time, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most influential moments that the whole world experienced in unison for me fall into two groups, dreams and nightmares. The post above me is fantastic and I want to give credit because 9/11 is a moment that really changed how the world works, the outlook people hold, and it clearly separates the generations who grew up before that day and the generation who has never know a time or world without that influence. I've been doing some work on &quot;Major Moments in History&quot; for a vampire game I'm planning because an important theme is that mortals are responsible for history, kindred react.<br /> <br /> This is weirdly relevant because depending on how strict you are to canon the whole beauty of the Resurgence is the human wonder brought about by the accomplishments of humanity... any possibly the shared horror at the atrocities we commit against our fellow man. I've adapted my list to also include moments that could be used as triggers for a different Resurgence, the appearance of Thallain Sidhe.<br /> <hr /><i>(My criteria for an event is that it had to have been experienced the world over, and to have the world mostly share the same emotion of wonder, horror, or a weird mix.)</i><br /> <br /> <b>August 6th to 9th, 1945 - Atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki</b><br /> The first bomb and second bomb allow for cracks in the structure of reality letting out a few normal Sidhe after Hiroshima until the bombing of Nagasaki then shifts these cracks only allowing those with two Unseelie Legacies to slowly break free... Thallain Sidhe.<br /> <br /> <b>October 4th, 1957 - Sputnik 1</b><br /> This was a trigger for fear in the states, joy back in Russia, and most interesting in my opinion is how the world over had the shared experience of listening to this faint beeping since all it took was a radio to pick up on it.<br /> <br /> <b>October 14th to 28th, 1962 - Cuban Missile Crisis</b><br /> The whole world sits on the edge during a time when, even more than usual, the idea of humanity destroying itself because a realistic possibility that potentially was about to occur.<br /> <br /> Berlin Wall works as does the 1979 Iranian Revolution if you want to have a major world event that is different from the usually western focused ones often used.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3161-goliath","name":"Goliath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}